Admissions
The admissions team interacts directly with prospective students, parents, applicants, alumni, staff, and faculty to provide services and support that lead to a positive student experience. The team is responsible for:
supporting a positive prospective student experience through incredible service, including through participation in recruitment initiatives;
making sure that the diverse domestic and international incoming class reflects qualified students;
ensuring that admissions decisions are made in a fair, consistent, and justified manner;
admitting students in a manner that supports student success and the University’s enrolment targets;
playing a direct role in the development and implementation of the institution’s Strategic Enrolment Management (SEM) plan and supporting the financial security of the University;

Enrolment services and academic policy
The enrolment services and academic policy portfolio is responsible for:
leadership for the strategic enrolment management of all currently enrolled undergraduate students;
accountability for the systems, processes, and office activities that guard the integrity and confidentiality of student records;
ensuring academic policy and requirements are accurately and consistently applied;
overseeing the scheduling of classes and final examinations, student-initiated services related to their academic records, and classroom renewal projects;
maintaining a productive working relationship with deans, associate deans, and university college principals/presidents as well as their departments and administrative staff; and
University representative to other Ontario universities and the Ministry of Colleges Universities, Research Excellence and Security.

